x</td><td>TF32</td><td>FP32</td><td>186</td></tr><tr><td>Matrix</td><td>INT8</td><td>INT32</td><td>186</td></tr></table>"}], "17": [{"bbox": [25.0, 49.0, 358.0, 114.0], "text": "## Tensix Core - Compute"}, {"bbox": [49.0, 204.0, 418.0, 362.0], "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td>Engine</td><td>Data Format</td><td>Accumulator</td><td>TFLOPs</td></tr><tr><td>Vector</td><td>FP32</td><td>FP32</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Vector</td><td>INT16</td><td>INT32</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Vector</td><td>INT32</td><td>INT32</td><td>6</td></tr></table>"}, {"bbox": [61.0, 636.0, 108.0, 696.0], "text": "Router\n\n0"}, {"bbox": [146.0, 492.0, 196.0, 558.0], "text": "RISC-V\n\n2"}, {"bbox": [221.0, 492.0, 271.0, 558.0], "text": "RISC-V\n\n3"}, {"bbox": [296.0, 492.0, 347.0, 558.0], "text": "RISC-V\n\n4"}, {"bbox": [174.0, 620.0, 219.0, 716.0], "text": "Tile\n\nMath\n\nEngine"}, {"bbox": [267.0, 620.0, 318.0, 716.0], "text": "Vector\n\nMath\n\nEngine"}, {"bbox": [379.0, 636.0, 427.0, 697.0], "text": "Router\n\n1"}, {"bbox": [206.0, 784.0, 281.0, 818.0], "text": "L1 Memory"}, {"bbox": [453.0, 24.0, 511.0, 57.0], "text": "tan_tile"}, {"bbox": [475.0, 73.0, 584.0, 107.0], "text": "leaky_relu_tile"}, {"bbox": [501.0, 118.0, 557.0, 151.0], "text": "exp_tile"}, {"bbox": [505.0, 186.0, 650.0, 219.0], "text": "```cpp\n\ntemplate<bool fast_and_approx = false>\n\nvoid ckernel::exp_tile_init()\n\n```"}, {"bbox": [510.0, 232.0, 648.0, 254.0], "text": "Please refer to documentation for any_init."}, {"bbox": [504.0, 276.0, 650.0, 309.0], "text": "```cpp\n\ntemplate<bool fast_and_approx = false>\n\nvoid ckernel::exp_tile(uint32_t idst)\n\n```"}, {"bbox": [509.0, 324.0, 968.0, 362.0], "text": "Performs element-wise computation of exponential on each element of a tile in DST register at index tile_index. The DST register buffer must be in acquired state via acquire_dst call. This call is blocking and is only available on the compute engine."}, {"bbox": [512.0, 371.0, 575.0, 388.0], "text": "Return value: None"}, {"bbox": [514.0, 398.0, 975.0, 478.0], "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td>Argument</td><td>Description</td><td>Type</td><td>Valid Range</td></tr><tr><td>tile_index</td><td>The index of the tile in DST register buffer to perform the computation on</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>Must be less than the size of the DST register buffer</td></tr><tr><td>fast_and_approx</td><td>Computation to be done faster and approximate</td><td>bool</td><td></td></tr></table>"}, {"bbox": [565.0, 586.0, 845.0, 668.0], "text": "General Purpose Vector ISA: elementwise, sort, re-shuffle, LUT"}, {"bbox": [683.0, 688.0, 708.0, 722.0], "text": "64"}, {"bbox": [616.0, 756.0, 770.0, 791.0], "text": "+ - $^{*}$ , sort, reshuffle, LUT"}, {"bbox": [682.0, 826.0, 697.0, 844.0], "text": "="}], "18": [{"bbox": [24.0, 50.0, 358.0, 112.0], "text": "## Tensix Core - Compute"}, {"bbox": [98.0, 158.0, 289.0, 190.0], "text": "1 user compute kernel"}, {"bbox": [98.0, 192.0, 441.0, 226.0], "text": "Automatically compiled to 3 RISC-V threads"}, {"bbox": [514.0, 43.0, 615.0, 69.0], "text": "transpose_wh_tile"}, {"bbox": [531.0, 80.0, 596.0, 107.0], "text": "reduce_tile"}, {"bbox": [546.0, 120.0, 575.0, 146.0], "text": "tilize"}, {"bbox": [562.0, 162.0, 658.0, 192.0], "text": "matmul_tiles"}, {"bbox": [564.0, 224.0, 990.0, 244.0], "text": "```cpp\n\nvoid ckernel::mm_init(uint32_t in0_cb_id = 0, uint32_t in1_cb_id = 1, uint32_t out_cb_id = 16, const uint32_t transpose = 0)\n\n```"}, {"bbox": [569.0, 268.0, 793.0, 287.0], "text": "Initialization for matmul_tiles operation. Must be called before matmul_tiles."}, {"bbox": [574.0, 320.0, 976.0, 434.0], "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td>Argument</td><td>Description</td><td>Type</td><td>Valid Range</td><td>Required</td></tr><tr><td>in0_cb_id</td><td>The identifier of the first input circular buffer(CB)</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>0 to 31</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>in1_cb_id</td><td>The identifier of the second input circular buffer(CB)</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>0 to 31</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>out_cb_id</td><td>The identifier of the output circular buffer(CB)</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>0 to 31</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>transpose</td><td>The transpose flag for performing transpose operation on B</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>Any positive value will indicate transpose is set</td><td>False</td></tr></table>"}, {"bbox": [547.0, 664.0, 609.0, 743.0], "text": "Library of\n\nLow-Level\n\nAPIs"}, {"bbox": [658.0, 646.0, 972.0, 681.0], "text": "Open source library of low-level kernels"}, {"bbox": [659.0, 682.0, 858.0, 714.0], "text": "1 API per math function"}, {"bbox": [659.0, 717.0, 908.0, 752.0], "text": "100s of tile & vector math LLKs"}], "19": [{"bbox": [26.0, 50.0, 354.0, 112.0], "text": "## Kernel Synchronization"}, {"bbox": [121.0, 177.0, 307.0, 214.0], "text": "Circular Buffer (CB)"}, {"bbox": [119.0, 218.0, 447.0, 295.0], "text": "- SRAM memory object with hardware enabled flow control"}, {"bbox": [564.0, 19.0, 982.0, 432.0], "text": "<table class=\"table table-bordered\"><thead><tr><th>Argument</th><th>Description</th><th>Type</th><th>Valid Range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>cb_id</td><td>The index of the circular buffer (CB)</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>0 to 31</td></tr><tr><td>num_tiles</td><td>The number of free tiles to wait for</td><td>uint32_t</td><td>It must be less or equal than the size of the CB (the total number of tiles that fit into the CB)</td></tr></tbody></table>"}], "2": [{"bbox": [25.0, 50.0, 140.0, 116.0], "text": "## Agenda"}, {"bbox": [105.0, 223.0, 302.0, 286.0], "text": "Architecture"}, {"bbox": [105.0, 386.0, 390.0, 454.0], "text": "Micro-architecture"}, {"bbox": [105.0, 552.0, 267.0, 618.0], "text": "Scale-out"}, {"bbox": [105.0, 718.0, 256.0, 782.0], "text": "Software"}], "20": [{"bbox": [485.0, 821.0, 963.0, 863.0], "text": "- Kernels for asynchronous pre-load / spill to DRAM"}], "21": [{"bbox": [23.0, 49.0, 364.0, 166.0], "text": "## All RISC-V Programmable Within the Ethernet Core"}, {"bbox": [624.0, 44.0, 707.0, 126.0], "text": "off-chip\n\nEthernet"}], "22": [{"bbox": [23.0, 321.0, 316.0, 434.0], "text": "## Scale-out"}], "23": [{"bbox": [26.0, 50.0, 551.0, 109.0], "text": "## Blackhole: Ethernet-Based Scale out"}, {"bbox": [32.0, 222.0, 284.0, 260.0], "text": "1 TB/s of Blackhole Ethernet"}, {"bbox": [32.0, 277.0, 346.0, 318.0], "text": "Can be connected into any topology"}, {"bbox": [32.0, 385.0, 284.0, 424.0], "text": "Mesh topology is great for AI"}, {"bbox": [69.0, 433.0, 383.0, 467.0], "text": "Locality and regularity of data movement"}, {"bbox": [69.0, 473.0, 190.0, 506.0], "text": "Sharded data"}, {"bbox": [70.0, 513.0, 293.0, 548.0], "text": "200 GB/s in N/S/W/E/Z"}, {"bbox": [69.0, 556.0, 190.0, 589.0], "text": "2D / 3D torus"}, {"bbox": [95.0, 957.0, 140.0, 977.0], "text": "Compute"}, {"bbox": [219.0, 959.0, 292.0, 978.0], "text": "Data Movement"}, {"bbox": [344.0, 958.0, 381.0, 978.0], "text": "Storage"}], "24": [{"bbox": [26.0, 50.0, 624.0, 111.0], "text": "## Blackhole Galaxy: 32 chips in a 4x8 Mesh"}, {"bbox": [41.0, 495.0, 294.0, 546.0], "text": "## 11.2 TB/s Galaxy I/O"}, {"bbox": [421.0, 374.0, 612.0, 412.0], "text": "X dim I/O: 8 x 200 GB/s"}, {"bbox": [393.0, 450.0, 623.0, 486.0], "text": "Y dim I/O: 16 x 200 GB/s"}, {"bbox": [422.0, 527.0, 620.0, 562.0], "text": "Z dim I/O: 32 x 200 GB/s"}], "25": [{"bbox": [25.0, 46.0, 743.0, 118.0], "text": "## Blackhole Galaxy: Scale-out \"Lego\" building block"}, {"bbox": [173.0, 159.0, 350.0, 278.0], "text": "24 PFLOPs \"AI compute\""}, {"bbox": [576.0, 158.0, 902.0, 277.0], "text": "16 TB/s BW, 1 TB capacity \"AI memory\""}, {"bbox": [393.0, 854.0, 557.0, 974.0], "text": "11. 2 TB/s I/O \"AI switch\""}], "26": [{"bbox": [23.0, 320.0, 291.0, 434.0], "text": "## Software"}], "27": [{"bbox": [32.0, 56.0, 590.0, 117.0], "text": "## TT-Metalium: Built for Al and Scale-out"}, {"bbox": [21.0, 187.0, 244.0, 220.0], "text": "- Kernels are plain C++ with APIs"}, {"bbox": [21.0, 279.0, 335.0, 3